append [SimTalk] - DataList
Appends the specified entry to the end of the DataList designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Plant Simulation does not allow to exceed the number of rows you set.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.append(Entry:any)
Parameter
The parameter Entry of data type any designates the entry you want to append.
Example
MyDataList.append("crankshaft")
See also
Number of Rows [lists]
append [SimTalk] - DataList
11-4228 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

appendList [SimTalk]
Adds the contents of all cells of the specified list to the DataList designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The contents of the existing cells remains untouched.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.appendList(List:any)
Parameter
The parameter List of data type any designates the list you want to append.
Our DataStack looks like this:
Example
var l: list[string]
l.create
l.insert(1,"one")
l.insert(2,"two")
MyDataList.appendList(l)
MyDataList.appendList(DataStack)
The content of MyDataList looks like this:
appendList [SimTalk]
