createNestedList [SimTalk] - DataList
Creates a nested list in the DataList designated by <Path>, containing lists and tables.
Remarks
The DataList has to be of data type list, stack, queue, or table.
Plant Simulation overwrites the existing sublist without moving existing list one row downward.
Local variables of data type list have to be treated differently as they cannot contain the data itself but only
references to the respective data structures. When entering the Method object, variables of this type do
not contain a reference to such a data structure yet (void). You can only access the data after the nested
list has been created.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.createNestedList([Row:integer, Name:string]) → list
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The optional parameter Row of data type integer designates the row of the cell. If you do not specify a
row, Plant Simulation adds the list to the end of the DataList.
• The optional parameter Name of data type string designates the name of the nested that is to be
created.
Return Value
The return value has the data type list.
Is the nested list (DataList, DataQueue, DataStack, or DataTable) that was created.
Example
MyDataList.createNestedList(1,"MyNestedlist")
