determineRange [SimTalk] - DataList
Resolves the actual list range for the DataList designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.determineRange(Range:listrange, byRef StartColumn:integer, byRef 
StartRow:integer, byRef EndStartColumn:integer, byRef EndRow:integer)
Parameters
The method assigns the boundaries of the list range to the local variables, which you specify:
• The parameter Range of data type listrange designates the range of the list.
• The local variable StartColumn of data type integer designates the number of the first column of the
range.
• The local variable StartRow of data type integer designates the number of the first row of the range.
• The local variable EndStartColumn of data type integer designates the number of the last column of the
range.
• The local variable EndRow of data type integer designates the number of the last row of the range.
Example
param a: any
var fromX, fromY, toX, toY: integer
if isListRange(a)
   myDataList.determineRange(a, fromX, fromY, toX, toY)
   print "{",fromY,"}..{",toY,"}"
end
// You can call this method like this: 
myMethod({*})
myMethod({1}..{*})
// range with a user-defined row index
myMethod({#7}..{*})  
See also
Specifying a Range of Cells [several columns] > Column index belongs to contents
